{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-29_companynewsreleasedatedoct.htm, sha256 d7daafa425147f6b4de2a344cdda06fbd394fbbb7d91e2d42f70ebbd05c295c3.\nEX-99.1 2 companynewsreleasedatedoct.htm EX-99.1\nBelden Reports Record Third Quarter 2026 Results and Announces $100 Million Data Center Agreement for 2027\nSt. Louis, Missouri \u2013 October 29, 2026 - Belden Inc. (NYSE: BDC) (\u201cBelden\u201d or the \u201cCompany\u201d), a global full-stack networking solutions company, today reported fiscal third quarter results for the period ended September 27, 2026.\nThird Quarter 2026 Highlights \u2022Record revenues of $966 million, up 38% y/y and up 11% y/y organically \u2022Record orders of $1,017 million, up 46% y/y and up 16% y/y organically, with a book-to-bill of 1.05x \u2022GAAP EPS of ($0.29), including non-cash purchase accounting charges related to the Ruckus acquisition \u2022Adjusted EPS of $2.26, up 15% y/y \u2022Reached agreement to supply $100 million of fiber solutions to major US data center customer in 2027\n\"Belden delivered another record quarter, with revenue of $966 million, up 38% year over year and 11% organically, and Adjusted EPS of $2.26, up 15% year over year. We also surpassed $1 billion in quarterly orders for the first time, with orders up 46% year over year and 16% organically, and a book-to-bill of 1.05x,\" said Ashish Chand, President and CEO of Belden Inc. \"Demand remains robust across our key markets as AI and automation drive continued investment in networking infrastructure, from the data center to the factory floor. Our data center business reached an important milestone, with a signed agreement to supply $100 million of fiber assemblies in 2027. With this announcement, we now expect our data center business to grow by more than 50% next year. Our Ruckus integration is progressing, and we are encouraged by the growing cross-selling funnel and positive conversations we are having with customers. Belden is increasingly positioned as a networking partner for physical AI and automation, and the momentum we are seeing gives us confidence in the opportunity ahead.\"\nThird Quarter 2026\nRevenues for the quarter increased by $268 million, or 38%, to $966 million from $698 million in the year-ago period. Revenues increased 11% organically from the year-ago period. Net income was ($11) million, compared to $57 million in the year-ago period. Net income as a percentage of revenues was (1.2)%, compared to 8.1% in the year-ago period. GAAP EPS totaled ($0.29) for the quarter, compared to $1.41 in the year-ago period, reflecting the addition of Ruckus and related purchase accounting estimates.\nAdjusted EBITDA was $171 million, up $52 million, or 44%, compared to $119 million in the year-ago period. Adjusted EBITDA margin was 17.7%, up 70 bps, compared to 17.0% in the year-ago period. Adjusted EPS was $2.26, increasing 15% compared to $1.97 in the year-ago period. Adjusted results are non-GAAP measures, and a non-GAAP reconciliation table is provided as an appendix to this release.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "GAAP results reflect purchase accounting for the Ruckus acquisition including non-cash charges of $100 million related to the amortization of acquired intangible assets and inventory fair value step-up. These charges are excluded from Adjusted EPS and Adjusted EBITDA, which management uses, along with GAAP results, to evaluate the Company's operating performance.\nOutlook\n\u201cOur fourth quarter outlook reflects strong underlying demand and the momentum we're building as one company with Ruckus,\" said Dr. Chand. \"Orders are at record levels entering the quarter, our solutions pipeline continues to build, and we're seeing growing engagement from data center and physical AI customers. We remain disciplined given the near-term macroeconomic and supply chain environment, but the long-term fundamentals across our markets continue to strengthen. Our focus remains on execution, integration, and capturing the opportunity in front of us.\"\nAssuming the continuation of current market conditions, the table below provides guidance for the fourth quarter of 2026.\nFourth Quarter 2026:\nGuidance\nRevenues (million) $960 - $980\nGAAP EPS $0.24 - $0.39\nAdjusted EPS $2.20 - $2.35\nEarnings Conference Call\nManagement will host a conference call today at 8:30 am ET to discuss Belden's quarterly results. The listen-only audio of the conference call will be broadcast live online at https://investor.belden.com. The dial-in number for participants is 1-800-330-6710 with confirmation code 6822993. A replay of this conference call will remain accessible in the investor relations section of the Company\u2019s website for a limited time.\nEarnings per Share (EPS) and Organic Growth\nAll references to EPS within this earnings release refer to net income per diluted share. Organic growth, a non-GAAP measure, is calculated as the change in revenues excluding the impacts from currency exchange rates, copper prices, acquisitions, and divestitures. Organic order growth i